@anon.9bf146a73cb71d9c7e3fe69f46c42f4a.723 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1374 x i8] }> <{ [1374 x i8] c"A footnote.\0A\0AIncludes additional remarks and references on the same page with footnotes.\0AA footnote will insert a superscript number that links to the note at the\0Abottom of the page. Notes are numbered sequentially throughout your document\0Aand can break across multiple pages.\0A\0ATo customize the appearance of the entry in the footnote listing, see\0A[`footnote.entry`]($footnote.entry). The footnote itself is realized as a\0Anormal superscript, so you can use a set rule on the [`super`] function to\0Acustomize it. You can also apply a show rule to customize only the footnote\0Amarker (superscript number) in the running text.\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0ACheck the docs for more details.\0A#footnote[https://typst.app/docs]\0A```\0A\0AThe footnote automatically attaches itself to the preceding word, even if\0Athere is a space before it in the markup. To force space, you can use the\0Astring `[#\22 \22]` or explicit [horizontal spacing]($h).\0A\0ABy giving a label to a footnote, you can have multiple references to it.\0A\0A```example\0AYou can edit Typst documents online.\0A#footnote[https://typst.app/app] <fn>\0ACheckout Typst's website. @fn\0AAnd the online app. #footnote(<fn>)\0A```\0A\0A_Note:_ Set and show rules in the scope where `footnote` is called may not\0Aapply to the footnote's content. See [here][issue] for more information.\0A\0A[issue]: https://github.com/typst/typst/issues/1467#issuecomment-1588799440" }>, align 1
